# GitHub reads this for its "Cite this repository" button, and Zenodo when it
# archives a release. Software indexes read codemeta.json. Edit this file only, then
# run `just citation` to bring codemeta.json in line; the citesync git hook fails while they or the package manifests disagree. Check the name split below:
# the first word becomes the given name.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: "r9lab-vocabulary"
abstract: "R9lab reference vocabulary: product types and component and material classes as SKOS, with crosswalks to CPC 2.1, UNU-KEYs, Wikidata and BAFU"
authors:
  - given-names: "Simon"
    family-names: "van Lierde"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6953-909X"
    email: "code@duinlab.nl"
repository-code: "https://github.com/simonvanlierde/r9lab-vocabulary"
license: Apache-2.0
